// A let of a block that ends in a generic name kept the cell that read was
// compiled as for its name's type, one level deep with the name's instance
// as a lower bound, where the check closed the instance as the scheme. A use
// copied nothing, so two uses at different types met in one cell: `a` was
// [i64, string] and `a + 1` was refused "i64 does not contain string". A
// block ending in the lambda itself was generic all along (soak nov24f).
// Expected trace (both engines): (2, "s").
{ let f = |x| x; let g = { 0; f }; let a = g(1); let b = g("s"); (a + 1, b) }
